  "landfallEstimate": "Movement towards Andhra Pradesh coast",
  "rawBulletin": "India Meteorological Department\n(Ministry of Earth Sciences)\nNATIONAL BULLETIN NO. 3 (BOB/10/2026)\nTIME OF ISSUE:1500 HOURS IST DATED:15.11.2026\nFROM: INDIA METEOROLOGICAL DEPARTMENT (FAX NO. 24643965/24699216/24623220)\nTO: CONTROL ROOM, NDM, MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS (FAX.NO. 23093750)\nCONTROL ROOM NDMA (FAX.NO. 26701729)\nCABINET SECRETARIAT (FAX.NO.23012284, 23018638)\nPS TO HON\u2019BLE MINISTER FOR S & T AND EARTH SCIENCES (FAX NO.23316745)\nSECRETARY, MOES (FAX NO. 24629777)\nH.Q. (INTEGRATED DEFENCE STAFF AND CDS) (FAX NO. 23005137/23005147)\nDIRECTOR GENERAL, DOORDARSHAN (23385843)\nDIRECTOR GENERAL, AIR (23421105, 23421219)\nPIB MOES (FAX NO. 23389042)\nUNI (FAX NO. 23355841)\nD.G. NATIONAL DISASTER RESPONSE FORCE (NDRF) (FAX NO. 26105912, 2436 3260)\nDIRECTOR, PUNCTUALITY, INDIAN RAILWAYS (FAX NO. 23388503)\nCHIEF SECRETARY, GOVT. OF ANDAMAN & NICOBAR ISLANDS (FAX NO. 03192-232656)\nCHIEF SECRETARY, GOVT. OF ANDHRA PRADESH (FAX NO. 0863-2441029)\nCHIEF SECRETARY, GOVT. OF ODISHA (FAX NO. 0674-2536660)\nCHIEF SECRETARY, GOVT OF TELANGANA (FAX NO 040-23455340)\nCHIEF SECRETARY, GOVT. OF TAMIL NADU (FAX NO. 044-25672304)\nCHIEF SECRETARY, GOVT. OF PUDUCHERRY (FAX NO. 0413-2334145)\nCHIEF SECRETARY, GOVT. OF CHHATTISGARH (FAX NO. 0771-2221206)\nCHIEF SECRETARY, GOVT. OF JHARKHAND (FAX NO. 0651-2400255)\nCHIEF SECRETARY, GOVT. OF WEST BENGAL (FAX NO. 033-22144328)\nSub: Depression over Southeast & adjoining Southwest Bay of Bengal [Pre Cyclone\nWatch for Andhra Pradesh & adjoining South Odisha coasts].\nThe Depression over Southeast & adjoining Southwest Bay of Bengal moved north-northwestwards with\nthe speed of 15 kmph during past 06 hours and lay centered at 1130 hours IST of today, the 15th\nNovember, 2026 over the same region, near Latitude 9.8\u00b0N and Longitude 86.8\u00b0E, about 620 km east-\nnortheast of Trincomalee (Sri Lanka), 680km west-southwest of Sri Vijaya Puram (Andaman & Nicobar\nIslands), 800 km east-southeast of Chennai (Tamil Nadu), 960 km south-southeast of Visakhapatnam\n(Andhra Pradesh) and 1070 km south-southeast of Gopalpur (Odisha).\nIt is very likely to move north-northwestwards, intensify further into a Cyclonic Storm over the central parts\nof south & adjoining westcentral Bay of Bengal on 16th November and into a Severe Cyclonic Storm over\nwestcentral Bay of Bengal on 17th November, 2026. Thereafter, it is likely to intensify further and move\nnorthwestwards towards Andhra Pradesh coast during subsequent 2 days.\nForecast location and intensity are given in following table:\nDate/Time Position Maximum sustained surface Category of cyclonic\n(IST) (Lat. 0N/ long. 0E) wind speed (Kmph) disturbance\n15.11.26/1130 9.8/86.8 45-55 gusting to 65 Depression\n15.11.26/2330 10.3/86.7 55-65 gusting to 75 Deep Depression\n16.11.26/1130 11.0/86.6 60-70 gusting to 80 Cyclonic Storm\n16.11.26/2330 11.7 /86.4 75-85 gusting to 95 Cyclonic Storm\n17.11.26/1130 12.4/86.2 90-100 gusting to 110 Severe Cyclonic Storm\n17.11.26/2330 13.3/86.0 95-105 gusting to 115 Severe Cyclonic Storm\n18.11.26/1130 14.1/85.6 105-115 gusting to 125 Severe Cyclonic Storm\n18.11.26/2330 15.1/85.2 115-125 gusting to 135 Very Severe Cyclonic Storm\n19.11.26/1130 16.2/84.7 120-130 gusting to 145 Very Severe Cyclonic Storm\nWarnings:\n(i) Rainfall Warning:\nAndaman & Nicobar Islands: Light to moderate rainfall at most places is very likely during 15th to 17th\nNovember.\nTamil Nadu, Puducherry & Karaikal: Light to moderate rainfall at many places with heavy rainfall at\nisolated places is very likely over North Tamil Nadu, Puducherry & Karaikal on 17th & 20th with heavy to\nvery heavy rainfall at isolated places on 18th & 19th November.\nCoastal Andhra Pradesh: Light to moderate rainfall at many places with heavy rainfall at isolated places\nis very likely on 18th, light to moderate rainfall at most places with heavy to very heavy rainfall at a few\nplaces over coastal Andhra Pradesh with isolated extremely heavy rainfall (\u226521 cm) over north coastal\nAndhra Pradesh on 19th & 20th November.\nOdisha: Lig",
